;; The JVM-only test namespaces are `.cljc` (this repo's test convention) but
;; reference JVM-only classes — `clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo`, `java.util.Base64`,
;; `java.time.*`, `java.nio.*`. clj-kondo also analyzes the `:cljs` projection of
;; every `.cljc` file, where those bare class symbols are structurally
;; unresolvable false positives: these tests never run under cljs (the DataScript
;; parity twin is a separate `.cljs` script run by nbb, not clojure.test). Scope
;; `:unresolved-symbol`/`:unresolved-namespace` off for those namespaces ONLY —
;; `src` stays fully linted, and every structural check (brackets, arities, unused
;; bindings) stays active everywhere. Same rationale as
;; kotoba-lang/kotobase-messenger's config, scoped per-ns instead of global.
{:config-in-ns
 {mail-archive.auth-test   {:linters {:unresolved-symbol {:level :off}
                                      :unresolved-namespace {:level :off}}}
  mail-archive.ingest-test {:linters {:unresolved-symbol {:level :off}
                                      :unresolved-namespace {:level :off}}}}}
